# Push → deploy watch (Syra)

## Hard gate (read first)

**Do not push, commit-and-push, or deploy unless this turn’s user message explicitly asks for it.**

Allowed triggers (user must say one of these, or clearly equivalent): `push`, `commit and push`, `deploy`, `/push`, or “push and watch deploys.”

**Not triggers** (finish the local work and stop; do not push):

- “ship”, “ship this”, “ship it”, ship-log, “make it live,” “done,” “finish,” “implement,” “fix,” “IMPLEMENT”
- Completing a feature, video, post, or production-bound fix
- Inferring that production needs the change
- Prior turns where the user once asked to push (history never authorizes a new push)

If the user only asked to commit (no push), commit only. If unclear, ask — do not push.

## When the gate passes — loop (mandatory)

1. **Push** to the tracked remote branch (`git push` / `git push -u` as needed). No force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly demands it.
2. **Wait** until both production deploys finish for the pushed SHA (or the newest production deploy after the push):
   - **Vercel `syra-v2`** (web → https://www.syraa.fun)
   - **Render `syra-agent`** (API → https://api.syraa.fun) when `api/` (or shared deploy-triggering paths) changed; if only `web/`/`documentation/` changed, still confirm Vercel, and skip Render only when the push clearly cannot trigger an API deploy
   - Also watch **Vercel `syra-documentation`** when `documentation/` is in the push
3. Prefer `node scripts/watch-deploys.mjs` (repo helper). If it is unavailable, poll with the CLI/API recipes below.
4. **On Error / build_failed / update_failed:** pull build logs, fix the root cause in-repo, commit (only if this turn already authorized commit/push), push again, and re-enter the wait. Repeat until **all required deploys are Ready/live**.
5. Soft cap: **5** fix→push cycles. If still red, stop with the failing platform, log excerpt, and the next fix to try. Do not claim success.

## Auth / tools (do not print secrets)

- **Vercel:** `env -u VERCEL_TOKEN` + CLI (`npx vercel` or `~/.local/lib/node_modules/vercel/dist/vc.js`). Auth via macOS `~/Library/Application Support/com.vercel.cli/auth.json`. Projects: `syra-v2`, `syra-documentation`.
- **Render:** `RENDER_API_KEY` from env, or Trancepad `backend/.env` if present. Service id `srv-d4i17q3uibrs73dtb6qg` (`syra-agent`).
- Never dump `api/.env`, tokens, or full auth.json.

## Success report (short)

- Commit SHA
- Vercel: Ready + production aliases (syraa.fun)
- Render: live (when watched)
- One-line note if a cycle required a build fix

## Do not

- **Auto-push** after coding, fixing, shipping assets, or “making something production-ready”
- Treat “ship” / ship-log / product delivery language as a push request
- Stop after `git push` without watching deploys (only applies when the user asked to push)
- Treat Queued/Building as done
- Skip the fix→push retry when logs show a clear in-repo build/runtime error you can fix (only inside an authorized push turn)
- Push unrelated dirty files, secrets, or `web/out/` promo dumps
